            {
                "entry_id": "66ca8caf-6ab8-3c07-a88d-54d50922512f",
                "word": "Kaohsiung",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9f9a874f-60eb-3e5a-b6fc-a940cfcbb442",
                        "entry_id": "66ca8caf-6ab8-3c07-a88d-54d50922512f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Deuxième grande ville de Taïwan."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4486ed47-7021-47eb-bc39-75695b96432f",
                        "source_entry_id": "66ca8caf-6ab8-3c07-a88d-54d50922512f",
                        "source_sense_id": "9f9a874f-60eb-3e5a-b6fc-a940cfcbb442",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kaohsiung",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kaohsiung",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                        "entry_id": "b0dee708-3986-362d-b1fe-3a2133a15a02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A city and special municipality in southern Taiwan, and the third largest city in Taiwan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b73d0d5a-ca74-4751-b1f1-e74ba5b76ffd",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "Although many factors in the industrial picture remain unfavorable, the Government reportedly is taking steps toward rehabilitation of industry. Repairs to the oil refinery at Kaohsiung (Takao) in Taiwan (Formosa) are being made, reportedly under the direction of engineers of the Anglo-Iranian Oil Company, under the auspices of the China Petroleum Corporation, a subsidiary of the National Resources Commission. This plant, formerly owned by the Japanese, was damaged during the war."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9440339e-d681-4cb6-bf12-90b690b1b216",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "The existing steel industry is centered at Kaohsiung and is based mainly on local and imported scrap. An integrated steelworks being built by CI&S, also at Kaohsiung, will have an annual ingot capacity of 1.5 million tons by 1977 and, it is hoped 6 million tons by 1983; the bulk of the raw materials needed will be from foreign sources. Meanwhile, large tonnages of finished steel produced are imported."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de9858f4-1be6-432e-8206-157c3392c1dd",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "Kaohsiung is the second largest city in Taiwan and has the biggest seaport."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebf90ea4-4cbc-41bc-98aa-a7562cf12a0d",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "The mayor of Kaohsiung, Chen Chi-mai, said the southern port city on Saturday also implemented new rules requiring face masks and social distancing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dda98512-3d60-4812-8e17-368f8929b79b",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "On Friday, three months after she moved in, Ms. Huang was feeling grateful not to be among the dead after a fire tore through the partly abandoned 13-story mixed-used building on Thursday night in the southern port city of Kaohsiung."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1196b8b4-eaab-48f4-838e-fdc2f124838d",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "Speaking to reporters in the southern city of Kaohsiung, Su said the \"new Taiwan model\" in combating COVID-19 was a \"normal life, active epidemic prevention and steady opening\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27a69e35-e936-4009-a83b-06deaec8bcce",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "A high-end IC packaging and testing plant in Kaohsiung owned by Advanced Semiconductor Engineering, Inc., a 100-percent-owned subsidiary of ASE Technology Holding Co., has been selected as a \"lighthouse factory\" by the World Economic Forum (WEF)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ac650f9-8337-40ba-a091-18c528509d89",
                                                "sense_id": "82360646-7c2f-3669-89bb-ba39628b7e54",
                                                "text": "Kaohsiung, a city on Taiwan's southern coast, is the 15th-busiest container port in the world. There would be global repercussions and immediate consequences for the Philippines should the port again be blocked by Chinese forces, as occurred temporarily in August following the visit of US lawmaker Nancy Pelosi to Taiwan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f380060-0795-371a-bcd8-9a71df071294",
                                        "entry_id": "b0dee708-3986-362d-b1fe-3a2133a15a02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A former county of Taiwan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14da3222-cba5-4434-a0a0-6ecee3cffa10",
                                                "sense_id": "8f380060-0795-371a-bcd8-9a71df071294",
                                                "text": "Occupying an area of 2,793, square kilometers, Kaohsiung county lists agriculture as its most important economic activity, followed by industry, commerce and fishing. While it is only 60 kilometers long, the county's coastline is extremely favorable to fishing activities. ¶ With its attractive mountain and seaside scenery, Kaohsiung county has enjoyed rapid development in the tourism industry. The best-known tourist attractions are the Chengching lake in the outskirts of Kaohsiung city, and Fokuangshan, where there are many Buddhist relics."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6650621-d17f-4c5e-9686-0b299e245580",
                                                "sense_id": "8f380060-0795-371a-bcd8-9a71df071294",
                                                "text": "Of the Four Great Ancestral Daochang, the Chaofeng Temple is the only one in the southern half of Taiwan; it sits on the slopes of Dagang Mountain in the Alian Rural District of Kaohsiung County."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
